[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: System Initialization
PREFIX: ZEP-SRS-12-

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: software_requirements.sgra

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-12-1
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: System Initialization
TITLE: Ordered initialization levels
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall support an ordered sequence of initialization levels executed during
system startup, comprising at minimum: EARLY, PRE_KERNEL_1, PRE_KERNEL_2, POST_KERNEL,
and APPLICATION.
<<<
USER_STORY: >>>
As a Zephyr RTOS user I want a well-defined and deterministic initialization order so that
device drivers, subsystems and application code can be brought up in the correct sequence.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-26

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-12-2
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: System Initialization
TITLE: Registration of initialization callbacks
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide a mechanism to register a function to be called automatically
at a specified initialization level and priority during system startup.
<<<
USER_STORY: >>>
As a Zephyr RTOS developer I want to register my driver or subsystem initialization routine
to be invoked at the correct phase of boot without modifying the kernel startup code.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-26

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-12-3
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: System Initialization
TITLE: Per-level initialization priority
STATEMENT: >>>
Within each initialization level the Zephyr RTOS shall invoke registered initialization
functions in ascending numeric priority order.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-26

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-12-4
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: System Initialization
TITLE: Return value handling during initialization
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall treat a non-zero return value from a registered initialization
function as an initialization failure and invoke the system fatal error handler.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-26

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-12-5
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: System Initialization
TITLE: Main thread creation
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall create a main thread that executes the application-provided main()
function after the APPLICATION initialization level has completed.
<<<
USER_STORY: >>>
As a Zephyr RTOS user I want my application's main() function to be called automatically
after the kernel and all registered subsystems have been initialized.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-26

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-12-6
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: System Initialization
TITLE: Idle thread creation
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall create a dedicated idle thread that executes whenever no other
thread is ready to run.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-26

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-12-7
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Non-Functional
COMPONENT: System Initialization
TITLE: Initialization executed in non-preemptible context
STATEMENT: >>>
Initialization functions registered at the EARLY, PRE_KERNEL_1 and PRE_KERNEL_2 levels
shall execute in a non-preemptible context before the kernel scheduler is active.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-26

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-12-8
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: System Initialization
TITLE: POST_KERNEL initialization with scheduler available
STATEMENT: >>>
Initialization functions registered at the POST_KERNEL level shall execute after the
kernel scheduler is active, allowing the use of kernel services such as semaphores
and mutexes.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-26
